# The build stage needs pom.xml and src/ and nothing else. Everything listed here either bloats
# the context sent to the daemon, breaks the dependency-layer cache on every unrelated edit, or
# would leak into the image.

# Host build output. Copying it in would also shadow the container's own target/ and can carry
# classes compiled against the host JDK 21 instead of the 25 the build needs.
target/

# Large and changes on every commit, so it would invalidate the COPY layer for no benefit.
.git/

# The live H2 database. Baking a copy into the image ships real conversation history and then
# gets silently masked by the ./data bind mount anyway.
data/

# Real secrets. The app resolves 'optional:file:.env' against WORKDIR /app, so a copied .env
# would be picked up by any container built from this image.
.env

# Editor and tooling state: no effect on the build, plenty of churn.
.idea/
.atl/
.codegraph/
